/E (TF: Isaac went from August 2018 until June 2019 and Victor went from August 2020 until June 2021. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
463 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 248 0 R
/E (MM: How did you first hear about the school?)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 248 0 R
/E (TF: We heard about it from a few mothers whose children had attended the year before. Remember- back then, the school was only two years old. Isaac went for year three. It was very new. After many conversations with those parents and from staff of the school, we chose Yeshivat Moreshet Yerushalayim because we felt it offered the right balance and environment for our family.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
465 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 248 0 R
/E (MM: Any special stories come to mind when you think back to your children's time at Yeshivat Moreshet Yerushalayim?)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
466 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 248 0 R
/E (TF: Yes, we can talk about two. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
467 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 248 0 R
/E (Isaac once needed to go to the hospital at 8:00 PM. It was the first time he would be there without any family. Rabbi Tessler personally drove him, stayed with him the entire night, and refused to leave until Isaac was discharged at 9:00 AM the next morning- despite Isaac repeatedly telling him to go home to his family and that he would be fine. Isaac remembers waking up and seeing the Rabbi sleeping on the chair next to him. Isaac tremendously appreciated this, and as parents that level of care is something we will never forget.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
468 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 248 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
469 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 248 0 R
/E (One story Victor remembers is how he and his friends wanted to go to Meron on Lag LaOmer, one year after the tragic incident when many people passed away due to overcrowding. A rabbi advised them not to go that day for safety reasons but promised that he would take them on a different day. He kept his word and took them on a special trip later which meant a lot to them.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
