/P 249 0 R
/E (TF: Absolutely. We saw meaningful growth in both their Torah learning and religious development, as well as in their personal maturity- handling responsibilities, managing tasks, and taking on new challenges with confidence.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (MM: As parents, what do you love most about the school?)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (TF: What we loved most was the great balance of work and play. We loved the structured learning, the business internships, the trips and outings, and the balance of weekends on campus and weekends off. The boys were given certain freedoms, but were always expected to conduct themselves properly and attend all required classes.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
